      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We report a case of aortic root dissection in a middle-aged male without history of recent trauma, presenting as a critical aortic regurgitation due to right cusp dislodgement. The intraoperative transesophageal echocardiogram revealed the \"double aortic valve\" sign suggestive of low dissection, which proved to extend to both coronary arteries."},
